# Review package: ticket 04, 8464f3f..b595300

## Commits
### b595300
perf(state): keep array writes off the object batch path

Once fill and copyWithin ran through the Proxy inside a batch, array
targets reached handleBatchFastPath, which had seen only plain objects.
Its [SUBSCRIBERS] load then deoptimized 36 times per 10-cycle run
(wrong map), and the case 'many dependencies', which runs after
'array fill (hookless)', got slower: +10.6% on medians and +6.8% on
totals over three interleaved A/B runs of 10 cycles against 87c8823
(A/A spread 4.3% and 2.4%).

Control: on 87c8823, with fill wrapped by hand in batch(), the same
slowdown and the same deopt pattern appear (2.2 ms against 1.8 ms on a
fill-then-many-dependencies sequence). The cause is arrays on the
shared batch write path, not the two names added to the method set,
its Set lookup or code layout.

handleBatchArrayWrite now serves arrays through a set trap of its own,
picked by one Array.isArray per state() call, shared with hooksSlotFor.
Interleaved A/B after the change: many dependencies -0.5% on medians
and -1.4% on totals, array fill -50.2%, no case slower beyond its A/A
spread.


